. Australia would use an entirely new squad in the final, while the United States subbed in two swimmers and China one."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The biggest surprise of the event happened on the first leg as " [:a {:href "/athletes/2504727"} "Yang Junxuan"] " came home in the lead over Australia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/140687"} "Ariarne Titmus"] ", who had won the 200 free the day before, in which Yang finished only fourth. China was never headed, maintaining the lead after every leg, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/141768"} "Li Bingjie"] " coming home for the gold medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Australia was second after three legs, but " [:a {:href "/athletes/129065"} "Leah Neale"] " could not hold off " [:a {:href "/athletes/126653"} "Katie Ledecky"] " on the anchor as Ledecky swam the fastest leg of the competition in 1:53.76 to get the United States the silver medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "People's Republic of China"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} "7:48.98 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "7:40.33 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "10"} [:a {:href "/athletes/2504727"} "Yang Junxuan"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/141769"} "Tang Muhan"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/129678"} "Zhang Yufei"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/141768"} "Li Bingjie"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/141775"} "Zhang Yifan"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/129663"} "Dong Jie"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazon